.TH LAMBDA-BILL 1 "2026-11-19" "lambda-bill 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lambda-bill \- estimate AWS Lambda on-demand cost from CloudWatch REPORT lines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
Estimate AWS Lambda on-demand cost from CloudWatch REPORT lines. Reads files only, no network.

Usage: lambda-bill [OPTIONS] <FILE>...

Arguments:
  <FILE>...  Log files, gzip exports, directories, or `-` for standard input

Options:
      --prices <FILE>       Price file. The default is the built-in first-tier on-demand list
      --arch <ARCH>         Architecture when the file does not say. `x86_64` (default) or `arm64` [default: x86_64]
      --function <NAME>     Function name when the file does not say one
      --functions <FILE>    JSON object of function name to architecture (`x86_64` or `arm64`)
      --headroom <PERCENT>  Percent above the memory base for the advice. An integer from 0 to 100. Default 20 [default: 20]
      --as-of <DATE>        Date for the price age check as YYYY-MM-DD. Default: today (UTC)
      --quiet               Print only the result and errors. No warning on standard error
      --verbose             Also print progress on standard error
      --output <FILE>       Write the report to this file instead of standard output. An existing regular file is replaced
      --json                Print JSON instead of the text table
      --md                  Print a Markdown table instead of the text table
  -h, --help                Print help
  -V, --version             Print version

Exit codes: 0 ok, 2 input or usage error, 3 --quiet together with --verbose, 130 SIGINT.
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
lambda-bill reads CloudWatch
.B REPORT
lines from local files and adds up the on-demand duration and request cost per function, for x86_64 and arm64.
It also compares Max Memory Used with the configured memory and suggests a different memory setting.
It reads files only, makes no network call, and uses no AWS SDK.
.PP
One
.B REPORT
line is one request.
The duration cost uses Billed Duration and the configured memory, with 1 GB equal to 1024 MB.
Init Duration is not added again: it is already inside Billed Duration.
A request id is counted once per function, and the report does not print request ids.
.PP
The built-in rates are the first-tier US East (N. Virginia) figures from the AWS Lambda pricing page, read on 2026-11-09.
Every report names the currency, the source URL, the date, the region label, and the tier.
The account free tier is not subtracted, and Provisioned Concurrency is not priced.
.PP
The advice assumes the billed duration stays the same.
A smaller memory setting also gives less CPU, so the function can run longer.
The advice is not a forecast.
.PP
A file can be plain text, JSON lines, a CloudWatch export document, or gzip.
Gzip is recognized by the bytes 1f 8b, not by the file name.
A directory is walked in sorted path order, and a symlink you name is followed.
The function name comes from the log group, then a header
.RB ( "# lambda-bill-function:" ),
then an
.I aws/lambda/<name>
path, then
.BR --function .
The default architecture is x86_64, which has the higher rate, so an unknown architecture is not underpriced.
A file larger than 268435456 bytes and a line longer than 1048576 bytes are rejected.
A JSON document, a price file and a functions file may hold at most 4000000 JSON values; a larger one is rejected before it is built.
A run reports at most 100000 function and memory rows (one per function, architecture and memory size); more is rejected with exit 2 and the message \fImore than 100000 function and memory rows\fR.
An error names the problem and does not print the text of a rejected line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B <FILE>...
Log files, gzip exports, directories, or
.B -
for standard input.
At least one is required.
.TP
.B --prices \fIFILE\fR
A price file that replaces the built-in rates.
It must be a regular UTF-8 file of at most 268435456 bytes.
The file records its own source URL and date.
.TP
.B --arch \fIARCH\fR
The architecture when the file does not say.
.B x86_64
(the default) or
.BR arm64 .
.TP
.B --function \fINAME\fR
The function name when the file, the log group, and the path do not give one.
It does not override a detected name.
.TP
.B --functions \fIFILE\fR
A JSON object that maps a function name to
.B x86_64
or
.BR arm64 .
It does not name the function.
It must be a regular UTF-8 file of at most 268435456 bytes.
.TP
.B --headroom \fIPERCENT\fR
The percent above the memory base for the advice.
An integer from 0 to 100.
The default is 20.
.TP
.B --as-of \fIDATE\fR
The date for the price age check, as YYYY-MM-DD.
The default is today (UTC).
When the date of the price file is more than 180 days before it, a warning with that date goes to standard error and the exit status stays 0.
.TP
.B --quiet
Print only the result and errors.
The warnings on standard error are not printed.
The report on standard output stays the same.
.TP
.B --verbose
Also print progress on standard error: a line per file argument and a closing line with the number of functions and requests.
Not allowed together with
.BR --quiet .
.TP
.B --output \fIFILE\fR
Write the report to this file instead of standard output.
The report goes to a temporary file in the same directory and is renamed over the target.
An existing regular file is replaced.
A symlink, a directory or a device at that path is refused, and a missing directory is not created.
Any failure exits 2 with one line on standard error.
.TP
.B --json
Print JSON instead of the text table.
The first key is
.B schema_version
(1).
Money and GB-seconds are strings.
.TP
.B --md
Print a Markdown table with the same amounts instead of the text table.
A
.B |
or a line break inside a cell is escaped.
Not allowed together with
.BR --json .
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print the usage text.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was written.
.TP
.B 3
.B --quiet
and
.B --verbose
were both given.
Nothing is read.
.TP
.B 2
An input or usage error: an unreadable or unsupported file, a line that does not parse, a bad option, or a sum that does not fit in a decimal.
Standard output that was closed or read-only at start, or a failed write, also exits 2 with a message; this includes
.B --help
and
.BR --version .
Every message goes to standard error.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT.
Nothing is written to standard output.
Standard error has one line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
lambda-bill examples/sample-report.log
lambda-bill --json --arch arm64 --function worker examples/arm-report.log
lambda-bill --function worker --functions examples/functions.json examples/arm-report.log
lambda-bill examples/export
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
README.md, QUALITY.md and SECURITY.md in the source tree.
